[quotes.thriving]
Wings wide open. Circling the good page.
So much light. I am dizzy with it.
This is the brightest you have been all week.
I could read this lamp forever. And you.
Drunk on lumens. Absolutely hammered.
The glow! The GLOW! Sorry. Got carried away.
I would fly into this page. Gladly.
Bright enough to die for. Moth talk. Sorry.

[quotes.content]
Resting on the spine, wings half out.
A steady glow. That will do nicely.
I have found a warm paragraph to sit on.
Do not mind me. Just basking.
Comfortable. Mildly luminous. Content.
Not a bonfire, but I will take a candle.
I have eaten one page. Tell no one.
Perched. Fuzzy. Fine.

[quotes.peckish]
Wings folded in. I have lost the light.
It has gone rather dim in here.
I am circling nothing. It is embarrassing.
A little glow? Any glow? No?
Bit dark, this. Bit bloody dark.
I flew into a wall. No light to blame.
One day unlit. My whole thing is light.
Come on. Throw a moth a paragraph.

[quotes.neglected]
Wings shut tight. Have not moved in days.
I have mistaken a dead lamp for hope.
Dark. Very dark. Moths hate this.
Do moths dream? Only of unread books.
Pitch black and pissed off about it.
I have started eating the curtains. Your fault.
No light. No point. No wings worth opening.
The dark night of the moth soul.

[quotes.milestone]
Brightest streak yet. I am incandescent.
A new record. I could fly into the sun.
Best run yet. My wings cannot cope.
Personal best. Absolutely luminous of you.
